    shadow: 'Habitual reticence can read as coldness, arrogance or hidden contempt, and it starves relationships of the self-disclosure that builds intimacy. Teams that run on few words make worse decisions because nobody shares what they know. With friends, partners and colleagues you need to trust, saying more, including doubts and feelings, is usually the stronger move.',
    honest: 'Speak with purpose: say what you mean, then stop. Listening more than you talk is generous as well as shrewd, and choosing your words carefully is a form of respect.',
    question: 'In your last difficult conversation, what did you say that you wish you had kept to yourself, and why did you say it?',
